Z||000000||KitKar||08-25-2000||06:16 PM||||I am sure this has been brought up before, but is it possible to the supercharger on a non S/C 3800 Series II? If so, are there any serious problems?<BR>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||08-25-2000||06:39 PM||||Depends on what you mean by *serious*. <P>Do you mean, put the stock Eaton on the engine or some aftermarket blower?<P>You will need so many parts that you will wish you had just gotten an SC engine int he first place. This applies to the Series I and II engines.<P>On a Series I, it's not worth the trouble. <P>On a Series II, it might not be so bad. I have both, but I've never compared an NA and SC Series II engine.<P>Medium miles 92-95 Series I SC engines (~50k) can be had for under $1000. <P>IMHO......<P><BR>||||reg||13
Z||000002||the need for speed||08-26-2000||01:44 PM||||were does some one start looking for a sc 3800 II  thats in good condition, 96 and up and whats a good price from your experience ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||08-26-2000||09:38 PM||||Copartfinder.com<P>Look for VIN with a 1 in the 8th position.<P>Pontiac Bonneville SSEi, Buick Park Avenue Ultra, Olds L88/98 LSS, Grand Prix GTP, Buick Le Sabre.<P>Don't rule out the Series I engines (92-95). <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-26-2000).]||||reg||1
